06:01 David again gathered together all the chosen men of Yisra'el, thirty thousand.
06:02 David arose, and went with all the people who were with him, from Ba`ale-Yeudah, to bring up from there the ark of G-D, which is called by the Name, even the name of HaSHEM-Tzva'ot who sits above the Keruvim.
06:03 They set the ark of G-D on a new cart, and brought it out of the house of Avinadav that was in the hill: and Uzzah and Achyo, the sons of Avinadav, drove the new cart.
06:04 They brought it out of the house of Avinadav, which was in the hill, with the ark of G-D: and Achyo went before the ark.
06:05 David and all the house of Yisra'el played before HaSHEM with all manner of instruments made of fir-wood, and with harps, and with psalteries, and with tambourines, and with castanets, and with cymbals.
06:06 When they came to the threshing floor of Nakhon, Uzzah put forth his hand to the ark of G-D, and took hold of it; for the oxen stumbled.
06:07 The anger of HaSHEM was kindled against Uzzah; and G-D struck him there for his error; and there he died by the ark of G-D.
06:08 David was displeased, because HaSHEM had broken forth on Uzzah; and he called that place Peretz-Uzzah, to this day.
06:09 David was afraid of HaSHEM that day; and he said, How shall the ark of HaSHEM come to me?
06:10 So David would not remove the ark of HaSHEM to him into the city of David; but David carried it aside into the house of `Oved-'Edom the Gittite.
06:11 The ark of HaSHEM remained in the house of `Oved-'Edom the Gittite three months: and HaSHEM blessed `Oved-'Edom, and all his house.
06:12 It was told king David, saying, HaSHEM has blessed the house of `Oved-'Edom, and all that pertains to him, because of the ark of G-D. David went and brought up the ark of G-D from the house of `Oved-'Edom into the city of David with joy.
06:13 It was so, that, when those who bore the ark of HaSHEM had gone six paces, he sacrificed an ox and a fattened calf.
06:14 David danced before HaSHEM with all his might; and David was girded with a linen efod.
06:15 So David and all the house of Yisra'el brought up the ark of HaSHEM with shouting, and with the sound of the shofar.
06:16 It was so, as the ark of HaSHEM came into the city of David, that Mikhal the daughter of Sha'ul looked out at the window, and saw king David leaping and dancing before HaSHEM; and she despised him in her heart.
06:17 They brought in the ark of HaSHEM, and set it in its place, in the midst of the tent that David had pitched for it; and David offered burnt offerings and peace-offerings before HaSHEM.
06:18 When David had made an end of offering the burnt offering and the peace-offerings, he blessed the people in the name of HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
06:19 He dealt among all the people, even among the whole multitude of Yisra'el, both to men and women, to everyone a cake of bread, and a portion of flesh, and a cake of raisins. So all the people departed everyone to his house.
06:20 Then David returned to bless his household. Mikhal the daughter of Sha'ul came out to meet David, and said, How glorious was the king of Yisra'el today, who uncovered himself today in the eyes of the handmaids of his servants, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovers himself!
06:21 David said to Mikhal, It was before HaSHEM, who chose me above your father, and above all his house, to appoint me prince over the people of HaSHEM, over Yisra'el: therefore will I play before HaSHEM.
06:22 I will be yet more vile than this, and will be base in my own sight: but of the handmaids of whom you have spoken, of them shall I be had in honor.
06:23 Mikhal the daughter of Sha'ul had no child to the day of her death.  
07:01 It happened, when the king lived in his house, and HaSHEM had given him rest from all his enemies round about,
07:02 that the king said to Natan the prophet, See now, I dwell in a house of cedar, but the ark of G-D dwells within curtains.
07:03 Natan said to the king, Go, do all that is in your heart; for HaSHEM is with you.
07:04 It happened the same night, that the word of HaSHEM came to Natan, saying,
07:05 Go and tell my servant David, Thus says HaSHEM, Shall you build me a house for me to dwell in?
07:06 for I have not lived in a house since the day that I brought up the children of Yisra'el out of Mitzrayim, even to this day, but have walked in a tent and in a tent.
07:07 In all places in which I have walked with all the children of Yisra'el, spoke I a word with any of the tribes of Yisra'el, whom I commanded to be shepherd of my people Yisra'el, saying, Why have you not built me a house of cedar?
07:08 Now therefore thus shall you tell my servant David, Thus says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, I took you from the sheep pen, from following the sheep, that you should be prince over my people, over Yisra'el;
07:09 and I have been with you wherever you went, and have cut off all your enemies from before you; and I will make you a great name, like the name of the great ones who are in the earth.
07:10 I will appoint a place for my people Yisra'el, and will plant them, that they may dwell in their own place, and be moved no more; neither shall the children of wickedness afflict them any more, as at the first,
07:11 and as from the day that I commanded judges to be over my people Yisra'el; and I will cause you to rest from all your enemies. Moreover HaSHEM tells you that HaSHEM will make you a house.
07:12 When your days are fulfilled, and you shall sleep with your fathers, I will set up your seed after you, who shall proceed out of your bowels, and I will establish his kingdom.
07:13 He shall build a house for my name, and I will establish the throne of his kingdom forever.
07:14 I will be his father, and he shall be my son: if he commit iniquity, I will chasten him with the rod of men, and with the stripes of the children of men;
07:15 but my lovingkindness shall not depart from him, as I took it from Sha'ul, whom I put away before you.
07:16 Your house and your kingdom shall be made sure for ever before you: your throne shall be established forever.
07:17 According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Natan speak to David.
07:18 Then David the king went in, and sat before HaSHEM; and he said, Who am I, L-rd HaSHEM, and what is my house, that you have brought me thus far?
07:19 This was yet a small thing in your eyes, L-rd HaSHEM; but you have spoken also of your servant's house for a great while to come; and this too after the manner of men, L-rd HaSHEM!
07:20 What can David say more to you? for you know your servant, L-rd HaSHEM.
07:21 For your word's sake, and according to your own heart, have you worked all this greatness, to make your servant know it.
07:22 Therefore you are great, HaSHEM G-D: for there is none like you, neither is there any G-D besides you, according to all that we have heard with our ears.
07:23 What one nation in the earth is like your people, even like Yisra'el, whom G-D went to redeem to himself for a people, and to make him a name, and to do great things for you, and awesome things for your land, before your people, whom you redeem to you out of Mitzrayim, from the nations and their gods?
07:24 You did establish to yourself your people Yisra'el to be a people to you forever; and you, HaSHEM, became their G-D.
07:25 Now, HaSHEM G-D, the word that you have spoken concerning your servant, and concerning his house, confirm you it forever, and do as you have spoken.
07:26 Let your name be magnified forever, saying, HaSHEM-Tzva'ot is G-D over Yisra'el; and the house of your servant David shall be established before you.
07:27 For you, HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, the G-D of Yisra'el, have revealed to your servant, saying, I will build you a house: therefore has your servant found in his heart to pray this prayer to you.
07:28 Now, O L-rd HaSHEM, you are G-D, and your words are truth, and you have promised this good thing to your servant:
07:29 now therefore let it please you to bless the house of your servant, that it may continue forever before you; for you, L-rd HaSHEM, have spoken it: and with your blessing let the house of your servant be blessed forever.  
22:01 David spoke to HaSHEM the words of this song in the day that HaSHEM delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Sha'ul:
22:02 and he said, HaSHEM is my rock, and my fortress, and my deliverer, even mine;
22:03 God, my rock, in him will I take refuge; My shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge; My savior, you save me from violence.
22:04 I will call on HaSHEM, who is worthy to be praised: So shall I be saved from my enemies.
22:05 For the waves of death compassed me; The floods of ungodliness made me afraid:
22:06 The cords of She'ol were round about me; The snares of death came on me.
22:07 In my distress I called on HaSHEM; Yes, I called to my G-D: He heard my voice out of his temple, My cry came into his ears.
22:08 Then the earth shook and trembled, The foundations of Heaven quaked Were shaken, because he was angry.
22:09 There went up a smoke out of his nostrils, Fire out of his mouth devoured: Coals were kindled by it.
22:10 He bowed the heavens also, and came down; Thick darkness was under his feet.
22:11 He rode on a Keruv, and did fly; Yes, he was seen on the wings of the wind.
22:12 He made darkness pavilions round about him, Gathering of waters, thick clouds of the skies.
22:13 At the brightness before him Coals of fire were kindled. 
22:14 HaSHEM thundered from Heaven, The Elyon uttered his voice.
22:15 He sent out arrows, and scattered them; Lightning, and confused them.
22:16 Then the channels of the sea appeared, The foundations of the world were laid bare, By the rebuke of HaSHEM, At the blast of the breath of his nostrils.
22:17 He sent from on high, he took me; He drew me out of many waters; 
22:18 He delivered me from my strong enemy, From those who hated me; for they were too mighty for me.
22:19 They came on me in the day of my calamity; But HaSHEM was my stay.
22:20 He brought me forth also into a large place; He delivered me, because he delighted in me.
22:21 HaSHEM rewarded me according to my righteousness; According to the cleanness of my hands has he recompensed me.
22:22 For I have kept the ways of HaSHEM, And have not wickedly departed from my G-D.
22:23 For all his ordinances were before me; As for his statutes, I did not depart from them.
22:24 I was also perfect toward him; I kept myself from my iniquity.
22:25 Therefore has HaSHEM recompensed me according to my righteousness, According to my cleanness in his eyesight.
22:26 With the merciful you will show yourself merciful; With the perfect man you will show yourself perfect;
22:27 With the pure you will show yourself pure; With the crooked you will show yourself shrewd.
22:28 The afflicted people you will save; But your eyes are on the haughty, that you may bring them down.
22:29 For you are my lamp, HaSHEM; HaSHEM will lighten my darkness.
22:30 For by you I run on a troop; By my G-D do I leap over a wall.
22:31 As for G-D, his way is perfect: The word of HaSHEM is tried; He is a shield to all those who take refuge in him.
22:32 For who is G-D, save HaSHEM? Who is a rock, save our G-D?
22:33 God is my strong fortress; He guides the perfect in his way.
22:34 He makes his feet like hinds' feet, Sets me on my high places.
22:35 He teaches my hands to war, So that my arms do bend a bow of brass.
22:36 You have also given me the shield of your salvation; Your gentleness has made me great.
22:37 You have enlarged my steps under me; My feet have not slipped.
22:38 I have pursued my enemies, and destroyed them; Neither did I turn again until they were consumed.
22:39 I have consumed them, and struck them through, so that they can't arise: Yes, they are fallen under my feet.
22:40 For you have girded me with strength to the battle; You have subdued under me those who rose up against me.
22:41 You have also made my enemies turn their backs to me, That I might cut off those who hate me.
22:42 They looked, but there was none to save; Even to HaSHEM, but he didn't answer them.
22:43 Then did I beat them small as the dust of the earth, I did crush them as the mire of the streets, and did spread them abroad.
22:44 You also have delivered me from the strivings of my people; You have kept me to be the head of the nations: A people whom I have not known shall serve me.
22:45 The foreigners shall submit themselves to me: As soon as they hear of me, they shall obey me.
22:46 The foreigners shall fade away, Shall come trembling out of their close places.
22:47 HaSHEM lives; Blessed be my rock; Exalted be G-D, the rock of my salvation,
22:48 Even the G-D who executes vengeance for me, Who brings down peoples under me,
22:49 Who brings me forth from my enemies: Yes, you lift me up above those who rise up against me; You deliver me from the violent man.
22:50 Therefore I will give thanks to you, HaSHEM, among the nations, Will sing praises to your name.
22:51 Great deliverance gives he to his king, Shows lovingkindness to his anointed, To David and to his seed, forevermore.
